DO NOT modify any files. Output text only. Role: BUILDER. You are designing a test battery for an SMS booking pathway that extracts dates from patient messages. The small extraction model reads the patient's message and writes a date phrase into a variable called preference_from. It is known to sometimes INVENT weekdays (e.g. patient says 'tomorrow july 28th' and the model writes 'thursday' instead of copying the date). Reference date is Monday 2026-07-27 Eastern. Design a battery of exactly 21 date phrases a real patient might type in an SMS, with the EXPECTED correct value of preference_from for each. The categories MUST include: (1) explicit month+day with ordinal ('july 28th'), (2) explicit month+day without ordinal ('july 28'), (3) relative word ('tomorrow'), (4) bare weekday ('tuesday'), (5) weekday with qualifier ('tuesday next week'), (6) compound with redundant cues ('tomorrow july 28th' -- Kenneth's exact case), (7) compound with conflicting cues ('thursday july 28th' where 28th is actually Tuesday), (8) vague/ambiguous ('sometime next week'), (9) shorthand/texting style ('tues nxt wk'), (10) bilingual/Chinese if relevant. For each phrase give: the exact patient text, what a CORRECT model should write in preference_from, and what date (MM/DD/YYYY) the gateway should resolve to (using Monday 2026-07-27 as reference). Output as a JSON array of objects with keys: patient_text, expected_pref_from, expected_resolved_date, category, risk_level (low/medium/high where high means the model is likely to corrupt it). No prose, just the JSON array.
